    course: "BI110",
    term: "T2",
    front: "What is taxonomy?",
    back: "## Definition and Functions of Taxonomy\n\n**Taxonomy is the branch of biology concerned with the identification, description, naming and classification of organisms.**\n\nIt provides a systematic framework for recognising organisms, assigning stable scientific names, and grouping them according to shared characters and evolutionary relationships.\n\nWithout a shared taxonomic system, the same species could carry different names in different regions, and researchers could not be sure they were studying the same organism. Taxonomy makes precise scientific communication possible across languages and countries.\n\n> Taxonomy covers identification, naming and classification together, not naming alone."
