    front: "Which Swedish botanist is widely recognised as the father of modern taxonomy?",
    back: "## Carl Linnaeus\n\n**Carl Linnaeus, an eighteenth-century Swedish botanist, is widely recognised as the father of modern taxonomy.**\n\nIn 1735 he published *Systema Naturae*, which introduced a nested hierarchy of ranks and the two-part naming system known as binomial nomenclature.\n\nLinnaeus established principles of hierarchical classification and binomial nomenclature that became foundational to modern biological naming. These principles continue to influence how newly discovered organisms are scientifically named and classified."
