    back: "## Domain to Species\n\n**From most general to most specific: Domain, Kingdom, Phylum, Class, Order, Family, Genus, Species.**\n\nEach step down narrows the group. A domain contains many kingdoms; a kingdom contains many phyla; and so on. Species is the most specific rank, it identifies a single kind of organism.\n\nA useful memory aid: *Dear King Philip Came Over For Good Soup*. Each word starts with the same letter as a rank.\n\nThe hierarchy is designed so that every organism can be placed at every level. This is why a house cat and a human both belong to kingdom Animalia, phylum Chordata, class Mammalia, but separate at order, family, genus, and species.\n\n> The sequence is fixed and is not reordered by modern taxonomy."
