    term: "T2",
    front: "Why was domain added as the highest taxonomic rank?",
    back: "## A 1990 Addition\n\n**Domain was introduced in 1990 by Carl Woese, over 250 years after Linnaeus built his system in 1735.**\n\nWoese compared ribosomal RNA from different organisms. The data showed that some prokaryotes are as different from other prokaryotes as plants are from animals. A rank above kingdom was needed to capture this split.\n\nThe three domains are Bacteria, Archaea, and Eukaryota. Before 1990, textbooks placed all prokaryotes in one kingdom called Monera. When the molecular evidence came in, that kingdom collapsed.\n\n> Domain was not invented by Linnaeus. It was forced onto the system by rRNA data that revealed a deeper split than kingdom can express."
